@startuml
scale max 1920 width
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
title Nearby Care Search and Hospital Sharing
actor User
participant "Nearby care UI" as UI
participant "Frontend Control" as FC
participant "HospitalRouter / ChatRouter" as API
participant "CheckNearbyHospital" as HC
participant "Hospital API boundary" as HB
participant "Holiday lookup" as Holiday
participant "ManageLinkedChat" as Chat
database "Messages + notification jobs" as DB

User -> UI : Open hospital search (home or chat)
UI --> User : Specialty selection, including explicit All
note over UI,FC
  No GPS or hospital query before selection; leaving does not search.
end note
User -> UI : Choose specialty
UI -> FC : Search current GPS (300 m) or selected map area
FC -> API : authenticated GET /hospitals/nearby
API -> HC : validated coordinates and filters
alt Specific department selected
  HC -> HB : concurrent first-page location probes (center + four directions)
  HB --> HC : addresses for nearby administrative regions
  loop region pages within shared budget and deadline
    HC -> HB : department list (Q0, Q1, QD, pagination)
    HB --> HC : selected-specialty records
  end
  note over HC,HB
    On timeout, stop remaining region/page requests immediately.
    Keep previous candidates as partial; no successful page means failure.
  end note
  HC -> HC : deduplicate, filter radius, sort all candidates by distance
else All departments
  HC -> HB : bounded nearby location pages
  HB --> HC : cached or validated provider records
end
HC -> HB : selected details within remaining time and detail budget
HB --> HC : verified specialties and weekly hours
HC -> Holiday : legal-holiday classification (bounded wait)
Holiday --> HC : known holiday/weekday or unknown
HC --> UI : filtered results + partial/availability + region_scope_uncertain
opt Empty GPS results with usable calendar, within expansion budget
  FC -> API : retry same center/filters at 500 m, 1 km, then 2 km
  API --> FC : stop at first nonempty result or error
  FC --> UI : effective radius and result metadata
  UI --> User : adjust camera; briefly report expanded radius
end
UI --> User : shared map, list, favorite, call and directions
UI --> User : dismissible introduction; button-free warning at >= 3 km or partial results
note over UI
  Address sampling alone does not trigger the limit warning.
  Region uncertainty remains in source notes and empty-result wording.
  Partial results can also mean missing hours; do not label every cause a quota limit.
end note
User -> UI : Change specialty or date/status if needed
UI -> UI : Keep date/status drafts until Apply; retain chosen map area

User -> UI : Choose hospital in a linked conversation
UI --> User : Recipient, hospital and editable message preview
alt User cancels
  UI --> User : Keep composer; no message is sent
else User confirms
  UI -> FC : sendMessage(stable clientMessageId, hospitalId, date)
  FC -> API : POST /chat/links/{id}/messages
  API -> Chat : active participant + existing request check
  alt Existing successful request
    Chat --> API : original stored message
  else New request
    API -> HC : requestShareContext(id, date)
    HC -> HB : fetch verified details
    HC -> Holiday : date classification
    HC --> API : server-owned place snapshot
    API -> Chat : save verified context, not client display fields
    Chat -> DB : message + notification job in same transaction
    DB --> Chat : saved message
  end
  API --> UI : saved message / actionable failure
end
note over UI,DB
  Failed sends keep the selected place and client request ID for retry.
  Symptom/shortage prompts do not automatically open or send a place.
  Hospital hours are not an emergency-service availability guarantee.
end note
@enduml
